      "writtenOn": "2016-11-08T14:50:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tested this out and it didn\u0027t work quite right for me. connect() is not what raises SERVER_DOWN, simple_bind_s() raises it. If there is no user and password set (which is a valid configuration if anonymous binds are allowed), then this method skips attempting to bind and successfully returns a connection object. It fails later the first time it does try to bind, and the server returns a 500 instead of a 504. This could be fixed by just adding an anonymous bind if user and password aren\u0027t set.\n\nI saw another issue when use_pool is turned on, which is that ldappool eats the SERVER_DOWN error and raises its own, so again the server returns a 500 instead of a 504. I can just throw up a patch to make ldappool expose the error and then this will work, but I\u0027m curious if you saw that as well?",
